# AIOS Intake

This is how your AIOS gets to know you. Fill in the answers below (a sentence or two each
is plenty — bullet points are fine), then run `/onboard`. Sage reads this file, interviews
you for anything still blank, and scaffolds your `context/` files from your answers.

You can leave answers as `[Your answer here]` — `/onboard` will ask you those live. And you
can edit this file and re-run `/onboard` any time to refresh; it's idempotent (it backs up
the old versions first).

> There are exactly **7 questions**. That's the whole intake by design — short enough to
> finish in one sitting, rich enough to make Sage useful on Day 1.

---

## Q1 — Who are you, what do you do, and what should I call myself?

Your name, your role / what you offer, and the name you want to give your AIOS. The default
is **Sage** — keep it if you don't care.

[Your answer here]

## Q2 — Paste 1–2 things you've written recently. Don't edit them.

This is the one question with a hard rule: your **voice samples must be pasted, not typed
here.** Open your last email or post in another tab and paste the raw, unedited text. If you
write it fresh while talking to Sage, the sample is already shaped by the conversation. One
email + one post is ideal (or two of either).

[Your answer here]

## Q3 — What are your 2–3 biggest priorities for the next 90 days?

Name something concrete — a number, a deadline, or a deliverable. "Grow my work" is too
vague; "ship X by August" is right.

[Your answer here]

## Q4 — Where does the value of your work actually land, and where is it tracked?

Outcomes, results, money, impact — and the place you'd look to see it. (For a student: where
your progress or grades show up. For a founder: revenue + the dashboard. Whatever fits you.)

[Your answer here]

## Q5 — Where do you talk to people you work with, your team, and the outside world?

Email, chat, DMs, social — the day-to-day channels.

[Your answer here]

## Q6 — Where do meeting recordings, notes, and important docs live?

Your notetaker, drive, notes app, wherever the record of things ends up.

[Your answer here]

## Q7 — What's the one task that eats your week, and where do you track your work?

The recurring time-sink (Sage uses this to find your first automation in `/level-up`), plus
your task tracker / to-do system.

[Your answer here]
